BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 507.94 Tm (There exist rational numbers which are not natural numbers, and natural numbers which are not rational) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 492.04 Tm (numbers.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 476.14 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 460.24 Tm (Examples: sqrt\(2\), pi, 3, and 0 are all real numbers.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 0.05 0.16 0.51 rg 1 0 0 1 56 428.34 Tm (1.2  Rational Numbers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 56 409.49 Tm (A number which can be written in the form p/q, where p is an integer, q is a natural number and q is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 56 393.54 Tm (equal to zero, is called a rational number. The set of rational numbers is denoted by the symbol Q.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 373.59 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 357.69 Tm (Examples of rational numbers: 0.333..., 2/3, -7/5, 0, 5, -2, 0.2) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 341.79 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 325.89 Tm (Every integer is rational, because it can be written as p/1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 309.99 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 294.09 Tm (A rational number can be terminating or non-terminating in its decimal form.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 0.05 0.16 0.51 rg 1 0 0 1 56 264.19 Tm (1.3  Irrational Numbers) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 56 245.34 Tm (Another important class of numbers is the set of irrational numbers. If x is not a rational number, then) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 56 229.39 Tm (it is irrational. The set of irrational numbers is usually denoted by I.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 209.44 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 193.54 Tm (sqrt\(2\), sqrt\(5\), sqrt\(3\) are all irrational.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 177.64 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 161.74 Tm (The decimal expansion of an irrational number is non-terminating and non-repeating.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.05 0.39 0.9 rg 1 0 0 1 56 145.84 Tm () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 70 129.94 Tm (There is no general way of knowing whether a given number is irrational.) Tj ET
